#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEST DEPENDENCIES — INTENT
#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   - the runtime set, plus what the suite needs to import and drive the app
#
#   - resolved into requirements-dev.txt, which is a superset of requirements.txt
#
#   - regenerate with `make lock-python`
#
# It includes the runtime intent rather than standing beside it because pip
# refuses to mix hashed and unhashed requirement files, and two independently
# resolved locks would eventually disagree about a shared transitive version.
#
# Including the intent is not on its own enough to stop that: the ranges below
# resolve freely unless the compile is constrained by the runtime lock itself.
# `make lock-python` passes --constraint app/requirements.txt for that reason, so
# every shared package here is the version the image ships, not merely a version
# the same range allows.


-r requirements.in

